      "body": "\n\n\n\n## Overview\n\n  Align the hybrid-LB inference in the `vllm serve` CLI with the one in\n  `create_engine_config`: `--data-parallel-start-rank` alone no longer marks a\n  node as hybrid LB — the node must also be non-headless.\n\n  Headless nodes run no API servers, so hybrid LB (each node runs API servers\n  for its local DP ranks) can never apply to them. `EngineArgs.create_engine_config`\n  already encodes this (`if self.data_parallel_start_rank is not None and not headless:`\n  in `vllm/engine/arg_utils.py`), but the CLI-side inference in\n  `vllm/entrypoints/cli/serve.py` only checked `data_parallel_start_rank`,\n  misclassifying internal-LB secondary nodes (`--headless --data-parallel-start-rank N`)\n  as hybrid LB. This is a consistency fix, not a behavior fix — see Claims.\n\n  ## Claims\n\n  - **No behavior change for any valid launch configuration.** `is_hybrid_lb` in\n    the CLI feeds exactly two things: the LB-mode conflict check and the\n    `api_server_count` default. In headless mode `api_server_count` is already\n    forced to 0 before either is reached in a way that matters, so the\n    misclassification happened to be harmless today; this change makes the\n    classification correct rather than coincidentally harmless.\n  - Per-mode analysis:\n    - **Internal LB, primary node** (no `--data-parallel-start-rank`, not headless):\n      condition was and remains `False`; `api_server_count` still defaults to\n      `data_parallel_size`.\n    - **Internal LB, secondary nodes** (`--headless --data-parallel-start-rank N`):\n      previously misclassified as hybrid LB; now correctly `False`. Routing is\n      unchanged (`api_server_count == 0` → `run_headless`).\n    - **Hybrid LB** (`--data-parallel-start-rank` without `--headless`, or explicit\n      `--data-parallel-hybrid-lb`): unaffected — the new `not args.headless` term\n      is always true there.\n\n  ## Validation\n\n  - Traced every consumer of `is_hybrid_lb` in `ServeSubcommand.cmd()`\n    (LB-mode conflict check and `api_server_count` defaulting) to confirm the\n    per-mode analysis above.\n  - Verified the new condition is identical to the inference already used in\n    `EngineArgs.create_engine_config`.\n\n  ## Details\n\n  In `vllm/entrypoints/cli/serve.py`, when neither `--data-parallel-hybrid-lb`\n  nor `--data-parallel-multi-port-external-lb` is set explicitly:\n\n  ```python\n  # before\n  is_hybrid_lb = args.data_parallel_start_rank is not None\n  # after\n  is_hybrid_lb = (\n      args.data_parallel_start_rank is not None and not args.headless\n  )\n\n  The comment above the block is updated to document the headless exclusion and\n  point at the matching inference in create_engine_config.\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
